    "blurb": "Features an expansive Dark Star that segues into He's Gone, plus a smoking Bird Song and a powerful Playing In The Band. Jerry’s guitar is massive and Phil’s bass intertwines beautifully throughout the jams. Soundboard recordings capture the high‑energy performance with crystal clarity.",
    "review": "The September 10, 1972 Hollywood Palladium show finds the Dead locked in a combustible groove that still feels fresh after all these years. The first set builds momentum with a tight Playing In The Band and a luminous Bird Song that showcases Jerry’s soaring leads and Phil’s floating bass lines. The second set erupts when Dark Star launches into an exploratory marathon before flowing seamlessly into He's Gone, delivering one of the most compelling segues of the era. Highlights continue with a blistering Truckin' and a jubilant Sugar Magnolia that sends the audience home on a high note. Across all six soundboard sources the band sounds crisp and focused, making this night a standout example of early‑’70s improvisational firepower.",
